  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced capacity of tripartite constituents to promote compliance, improve OSH and eliminate worst forms of child labour through social dialogue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Occupational safety and health (OSH) culture among other Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work needs to be nurtured in the early recovery phase to mitigate occupational risks that expose workers to injuries and death.   
ILO will support the creation of such a culture through the Development of an OSH profile and its tripartite adoption. This will be also done through the training of trainers for labour inspection and OSH experts, compliance improvement at private factories, and the establishment of an OSH training centre in Adra Industrial Zone. This centre will be managed by the Damascus Chamber of Industry and will support synergies with available OSH training courses including with the General Federation of Trade Unions.</narrative>
  </description>
